 "literal": "Worthy people's companion having become, himself to conduct the capable man, enemies to do that which remains is nothing.",
 "translation": "There is nothing enemies can do to a capable man who lives as a companion of the worthy.",
 "modern": "தகுதியுடைய பெரியவர்களின் கூட்டத்தில் ஒருவனாகி வாழும் வல்லமை பெற்றவனை அவனுடைய பகைவர்கள் செய்யக்கூடிய தீங்கு ஏதுமில்லை.",
 "explanation": "This couplet highlights the ultimate security found in the company of the great. The word 'தக்கார்' refers to worthy people of high character and wisdom. When a person is capable of making himself a part of their group ('இனத்தனாய்') and living by their standards, he becomes unassailable. Therefore, there is absolutely nothing ('கிடந்தது இல்') that his enemies ('செற்றார்') can do to harm him.",
